<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yinchuan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xingqing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yinchuan is the capital of the Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> plain below the Helan Mountains. Under the name Xingqing it was the capital of the Western Xia empire of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanguts">Tanguts</a> from 1038 until the Mongol conquest of 1227. The Western Xia imperial tombs lie at the foot of the Helan Mountains west of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yinchuan.jpg" alt="Yinchuan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Jinfeng_District,_Yinchuan_(53724463112).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
